.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Factor A_k = Q_k R_k and multiply back in reverse order, A_{k+1} = R_k Q_k = Q_k^T A_k Q_k. Every iterate is similar to A, and the subdiagonal entries decay like |lambda_{i+1} / lambda_i|^k, so the iterates converge to an upper triangular Schur form with the eigenvalues on the diagonal. Production codes add Hessenberg reduction and Francis&#x27;s shifts; the result is what scipy.linalg.schur returns.">

